# ============================================
# Peekaboo Environment Variables
# ============================================
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual values
# NEVER commit the .env file to version control

# --------------------------------------------
# Supabase Configuration
# --------------------------------------------

# Your Supabase project URL
# Found in: Supabase Dashboard > Settings > API > Project URL
# Example: https://xyzcompany.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_project_url_here

# Your Supabase anonymous (public) key
# Found in: Supabase Dashboard > Settings > API > Project API keys > anon/public
# This key is safe to use in client-side code due to Row Level Security
# Example: eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_anon_key_here

# --------------------------------------------
# Notes
# --------------------------------------------
# - The EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix makes these variables available in your Expo app
# - Never use the service_role key in client-side code (it bypasses RLS)
# - These values are safe to expose in mobile apps due to RLS policies
# - For production, consider using Expo's environment variable system
#   or EAS Secrets for additional security

# --------------------------------------------
# Getting Your Credentials
# --------------------------------------------
# 1. Go to https://supabase.com/dashboard
# 2. Create a new project or select existing project
# 3. Go to Settings > API
# 4. Copy the Project URL
# 5. Copy the anon/public key (NOT the service_role key)
# 6. Paste them above

# --------------------------------------------
# Local Development
# --------------------------------------------
# After filling in your credentials:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill in your actual values in .env
# 3. Restart your Expo development server
# 4. Verify connection using: npx expo start

# --------------------------------------------
# Deployment
# --------------------------------------------
# For Vercel:
# - Add these variables in the Vercel dashboard under Settings > Environment Variables
#
# For EAS Build:
# - Add to eas.json secrets or use --env flag
# - See DEPLOYMENT.md for detailed instructions
